{"lc": 1, "type": "constructor", "id": ["langchain", "schema", "document", "Document"], "kwargs": {"metadata": {"source": "medlineplus", "title": "Itching", "url": "https://medlineplus.gov/itching.html", "review_date": "04/15/2026", "term": "itching"}, "page_content": ". To feel better, you could try:Applying cold compressesUsing moisturizing lotionsTaking lukewarm or oatmeal bathsUsing over-the-counter hydrocortisone cream or antihistaminesAvoiding scratching, wearing irritating fabrics, and exposure to high heat and humidityContact your health care provider if your itching is severe, does not go away after a few weeks, or does not have an apparent cause. You may need other treatments, such as medicines or light therapy. If you have an underlying disease that is causing the itching, treating that disease may help.", "type": "Document"}}